{"type":"message","id":"1ba5069b","parentId":"75ff180a","timestamp":"2026-04-13T10:24:13.346Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Determining source maps**\n\nI'm considering whether I should include information that's inferred from the bundled section heading. I need to figure out if source maps are bundled together or if they exist separately as .map files. It’s important that I keep the answer concise but also actionable for better clarity. I'll make sure to focus on providing the most useful details in a straightforward manner. Let’s see how this can come together!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_05431021d9d8ba280169dcc43dd0548191a0d6deefe00a393a\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp3MRAnvs2nnB4BXYzSfJXdEhpYPWgj4WDVdyTj-S27xYbRijfJ3fnBQZiyDNcMB5WHA0tr7avTn9yc0Yfq8ORoZs3RGAkE-mDuENYhdz-fq47thDTOQQEIGALB0y-pEZD71cAaE3DcNCV7uvcZajE7j8lmAmBNOGnkJIWlRsDEV7TslKYOi9aHgCsMyST5E1Z_XrxKk6Dhvk8dCxG4E6dD_OxZy1I9Bbnt_SXD80qT07s7XOovXfjVeg6Yzrec3UoWpu-YgsSL2eZw9GuRpZCNG1xumxyRSKhnnHkEhJquAL9b2TnYigO4XI8TGdqz3V3WfW2rEJ5OL8jIgak5WyVT5er1LE_MYootyWKuDPWebULsTQEl40MSofoaMMbY_qGtVSVJnMU5iwOnxHl5kGRXutj11pnydUCsRtip-7j6L8PuNJPZroq6o_bx9nLqsMmete4Argftf5Bx_3BiytNjwKIaO9Q5RJuM-fijUM-AoxE1weV8SvqBF40-o0ddXAVD2kW4oc1F4TM1B1s29g6z05AzrkGSHWcBkylTOhCICdPyHo2nNj-cCmlZKJiuqnVSlPPGKettGTKwDlm7JCw8SjS31knSAY6aKcJewCNIGZEs7GyyItI-gD5jjsNBO1xVaMbozefjX0mxSWoegRcLaxymrYevkIB54iauV8bIeKhZIz0h1vDn74JZprRfybUgH4BtReonVicpFeaoo2z-YsiBIgRRxZTwrkhs8F7IzngMK_6NP2E6aKuZ0F7aG7d3X7-_t1dDIdTiEb0iT2Seo7hIXlA93bSL2UAFRotmRCkiEBHRLxh1AuborC7lUYGvenylxcsggQxjMRCzo11iG6BNVtvAdrQGyBiRZKXNSMRtgikT_n05BQVtz7ct8NPjPT8jnDQrfdtBXJQ7z3GCWNQ4g2TDw29hWMyyPuVTYBFsv7pH9UgzKErGphvKBIR3Fh3IFhoqI4MzeoUPJhY9hlPVfaxNfXHbhSF0nDIwQJkOqclO6h4Nfe5AtWSuH7mFWHRQmCZRlNk7DNvQHG8mdJHdw==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Determining source maps**\\n\\nI'm considering whether I should include information that's inferred from the bundled section heading. I need to figure out if source maps are bundled together or if they exist separately as .map files. It’s important that I keep the answer concise but also actionable for better clarity. I'll make sure to focus on providing the most useful details in a straightforward manner. Let’s see how this can come together!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I checked it end to end. The model print is generated by the **new/reset session notice builder**, and there is **no config toggle** for hiding just the model part.\n\n### What needs to be modified\n\n#### 1) Change the reset-session notice text builder\nThe current runtime code contains this function:\n\n```js\nfunction buildResetSessionNoticeText(params) {\n\tconst modelLabel = `${params.provider}/${params.model}`;\n\tconst defaultLabel = `${params.defaultProvider}/${params.defaultModel}`;\n\treturn modelLabel === defaultLabel\n\t\t? `✅ New session started · model: ${modelLabel}`\n\t\t: `✅ New session started · model: ${modelLabel} (default: ${defaultLabel})`;\n}\n```\n\nThis is the thing printing the model.\n\n### Minimal change\nReplace it with:\n\n```js\nfunction buildResetSessionNoticeText(params) {\n\treturn `✅ New session started`;\n}\n```\n\nThat removes:\n- `· model: openai-codex/gpt-5.4`\n- the optional `(default: ...)`\n\n---\n\n### Where it is\nIn your installed runtime, I found it in bundled files such as:\n\n- `/app/dist/reply-DmvM_nJj.js`\n- `/app/dist/config-C_HYv9DG.js`\n- `/app/dist/model-selection-BpQ-riKp.js`\n- `/app/dist/model-selection-PYX2f5gq.js`\n- plus several `/app/dist/plugin-sdk/...js` bundles\n\nThese are build artifacts, not a clean source tree.\n\n---\n\n### Important implication\nBecause OpenClaw is running from bundled `dist` files, there are **two possible ways** to change it:\n\n#### Option A — proper fix\nEdit the **original source** that defines `buildResetSessionNoticeText(...)`, then rebuild OpenClaw.\n\nMost likely source area:\n- `src/auto-reply/reply/get-reply-run.ts`\n\nThen rebuild/redeploy so the generated `/app/dist/...` bundles all get updated.\n\nThis is the correct long-term solution.\n\n#### Option B — quick runtime patch\nPatch the built `dist` bundle(s) directly.\n\nThat works, but:\n- it is brittle\n- it may be overwritten on update/reinstall\n- there are multiple generated bundles containing the same function, so patching just one may not be enough depending on which bundle your runtime loads\n\n---\n\n### What I found about behavior\nThe flow is roughly:\n\n1. you send `/new` or `/reset`\n2. OpenClaw decides to send a reset-session notice back to Telegram\n3. that notice text is built by `buildResetSessionNoticeText(...)`\n4. the result is routed out with `routeReply(...)`\n\nSo if your goal is **keep the notice, but remove the model print**, only the text builder needs changing.\n\nIf your goal were instead **remove the whole “new session started” message**, that would require changing the call path that invokes `sendResetSessionNotice(...)`, not just the text builder.\n\n---\n\n### Exact modification needed\nIf you want **only** this:\n\n```text\n✅ New session started\n```\n\nthen the needed code change is exactly this logic change:\n\n**from**\n```js\nreturn modelLabel === defaultLabel ? `✅ New session started · model: ${modelLabel}` : `✅ New session started · model: ${modelLabel} (default: ${defaultLabel})`;\n```\n\n**to**\n```js\nreturn `✅ New session started`;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Recommendation\nBest path:\n1. patch the source function\n2. rebuild OpenClaw\n3. restart the service\n\n### Short answer\nNeeded modification: **change the `buildResetSessionNoticeText()` function so it returns a fixed string without model info**.  \nIf you want, next I can tell you the **safest exact file/edit strategy** depending on whether you want to patch **source** or **installed dist only**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05431021d9d8ba280169dcc4406ed88191b8f32920e78f54be\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":184,"output":849,"cacheRead":80640,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":81673,"cost":{"input":0.00046,"output":0.012735,"cacheRead":0.020159999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.033354999999999996}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776075836853}}
